    "expectedFrames": "DERIVED FROM climbConcat, NOT from our reader. Grips encodes each hold as h{hole}p{role}[s{start}][e{end}] with explicit inclusive 1-based frame ranges (start defaults to 1, end defaults to frameCount) — an encoding with no delta semantics at all. Frame N is {placementId: roleCode} for every hold whose range covers N. Two encodings of the same climb, produced years apart by two different systems: agreement is evidence, not a restatement of our own decode.",
    "whyThisIsNotATautology": "On the reader this repo shipped before #3947, four of these five climbs decode to something else entirely; the pure-delta control is the only one that matches. After the fix all five match frame-for-frame, hold-for-hold, role-for-role.",
    "fullRunResult": "Decoding every multi-frame climb present in both catalogs: Kilter Original 35/112 correct before, 112/112 after; Kilter Homewall 15/29 before, 29/29 after. Zero climbs match the old reading but not the new one."
